# ByteBikri — copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# Nothing here is required for a local checkout: the demo runs on the
# development defaults and the local database. Listed in the order the config
# check reads them.

# ── Signing secrets (required in production; `npm run secrets` generates them) ──
# SESSION_SECRET=
# ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=
# AD_POSTBACK_SECRET=

# ── The public origin, and the operator account ──────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://example.com
# OPERATOR_EMAIL=
# OPERATOR_LEGAL_NAME=
# OPERATOR_ADDRESS=

# ── Database and email ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/bytebikri
# EMAIL_DRIVER=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=

# ── Video storage (VIDEO_STORAGE.md) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Where a store's VIDEO files are kept. Unset means local disk, which is the
# default: every byte stays here and nothing else changes. A host also DELIVERS
# the video to the viewer's browser — so a third party sees the viewer's IP
# address (the privacy notice says so), and a playback url is a bearer once it
# is in a browser. Identity documents and images NEVER go to a host, on any
# setting.
#
# One driver at a time, and the hosts are NOT interchangeable (VIDEO_STORAGE.md
# §10.1 has the table these lines summarise):
#
#   filemoon  a video host: a playback url per file, HLS or progressive.
#   gofile    needs PREMIUM — a free or guest account cannot produce a playable
#             link at all, so `upload()` refuses before sending bytes. Free
#             storage also expires after ~10 days of inactivity.
#   catbox    permanent and free, but 200 MB per file and progressive only; the
#             size cap is refused locally, before the bytes cross the wire.
#
# VIDEO_DRIVER=filemoon            # filemoon | gofile | catbox
#
# ── Filemoon (the host this product deploys with) ───────────────────────────
# FILEMOON_API_BASE=https://filemoon.org/api/v1
# FILEMOON_TOKEN=                  # `id|secret`, the whole token, as issued
#
# ── GoFile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GOFILE_API_BASE=https://api.gofile.io
# GOFILE_UPLOAD_BASE=https://upload.gofile.io   # uploads do NOT go to the API host
# GOFILE_TOKEN=                    # account token; the account must be Premium
# GOFILE_FOLDER_ID=                # optional: a destination folder UUID
#
# ── Catbox ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CATBOX_API_BASE=https://catbox.moe/user/api.php
# CATBOX_FILE_BASE=https://files.catbox.moe
# CATBOX_USERHASH=                 # uploads without it are anonymous AND undeletable
#
# Check whichever one is configured, from a machine that can reach it:
#   npm run video:check --prefix app -- --driver=gofile
